**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What a set of looks can recover of one target, and how far a tilt carries the wave off a plate's normal (001 §M 'It answers outright "this kit can never recover X"'; 'Snell caps the internal angle at arcsin(1/n_o) ≈ 40.4° for quartz, so more than one cut is required'; the S14.1 brief 'Snell caps the internal angle (REUSE MuellerInverse.internalAngle …)'). In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 467's declarations, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1: (1) `UnseenReason` = `NoLookReason` (there is no look: the kit holds no plate of the material, or no detector) | `AlongEveryPropagationReason` | `NormalIncidenceOnlyReason` | `NoRetardanceReason` | `FullMuellerNeededReason`, with `member this.text : string`, in that order: `no look of the kit measures a plate of it`, `every look propagates along its axes`, `it is seen only off normal incidence`, `no look carries its linear retardance or an oblique change of the Fresnel amplitudes` and `it needs a full Mueller polarimeter, or a polarizer and an analyzer around the plate`. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no wire tag. (2) `TargetSight` = `ReachableTarget | UnreachableTarget of UnseenReason`. (3) `type CrystalParameters with member this.targetSightOf (looks : PlannerLook list) (component : TensorComponent) : TargetSight`: `UnreachableTarget NoLookReason` for no look; `ReachableTarget` when some look's `sightOf this component` (step 467) is `SeenInLook`; otherwise `UnreachableTarget` of the first that applies, the reason naming what the looks lack closest to seeing it: `FullMuellerNeededReason` when some look answers `ReachMissesInLook`, `NoRetardanceReason` when some answers `NoRetardanceInLook`, `NormalIncidenceOnlyReason` when some answers `NormalIncidenceInLook`, and `AlongEveryPropagationReason` otherwise. (4) `member this.snellCap : Angle` on `CrystalParameters`: `internalAngle n IncidenceAngle.maxValue` (`MuellerInverse.fs:internalAngle`; `Fields.fs:30`, the steepest incidence the engine takes, 89 degrees) for n the smallest of the crystal's principal indices (the record's `RefractionIndex` itself, n_o or n_e, index1 to index3): the largest internal angle any tilt of a plate of it reaches, so a tilt never carries the wave further than this off the plate normal. No other member is added. Tests, in `PlannerReportTests` (step 467), over its probes and looks: `a target is reachable when any look sees it, and unreachable when there is no look`: the uniaxial n_e over a normal z-cut look and a normal x-cut look, both transmitted under `FullMuellerReach`, is `ReachableTarget`, and every uniaxial component over no look is `UnreachableTarget NoLookReason`. `an unreachable target takes the reason of the look that came closest to seeing it`: over the normal z-cut look alone the uniaxial n_o is `NoRetardanceReason` and g33 `AlongEveryPropagationReason`; adding a normal x-cut look under `EllipsometricReach` makes g33 `FullMuellerNeededReason`; the triclinic g12 over the three principal cuts at normal incidence under `FullMuellerReach` is `NormalIncidenceOnlyReason`; and each reason's `text` is its sentence above. `the Snell cap is the internal angle of the smallest principal index at the steepest incidence`: the uniaxial probe's `snellCap` equals `internalAngle (RefractionIndex 1.544) IncidenceAngle.maxValue` exactly, and the triclinic probe's equals `internalAngle` of its smallest index at `IncidenceAngle.maxValue` exactly.

**Acceptance.** After the target sight lands, `CrystalParameters.targetSightOf` MUST answer a target reachable when one look sees it and otherwise the reason of the closest look, and `CrystalParameters.snellCap` MUST be `internalAngle` of the smallest principal index at `IncidenceAngle.maxValue`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a target is reachable when any look sees it, and unreachable when there is no look`, `an unreachable target takes the reason of the look that came closest to seeing it` and `the Snell cap is the internal angle of the smallest principal index at the steepest incidence`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
